---
description: How the default agent reads live chord progressions from chords-and-tabs
alwaysApply: true
---

When the user asks what chords or progressions are in the current song, query the local agent API instead of guessing from source defaults.

1. `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:17891/progressions`
2. If that fails, read `~/.config/chords-and-tabs/progressions.json` (or `~/Library/Application Support/chords-and-tabs/progressions.json` on macOS).
3. Use `/song` or `song.json` only when you need empty slots or full structure.

The default starter song is not necessarily what the user has on screen. Always read the live snapshot.
